Conflicts: plasma-welcome
Description: Wild OS look and feel
 The Wild OS desktop as drawn in the Wild OS Design System: dark glass
 colour scheme, Albert Sans typeface, Glacier accent, floating taskbar with the
 tray at its right end, boot and sign-in screens, icons, default wallpaper
 and logo.
 .
 It conflicts with plasma-welcome because Wild OS ships its own first-run
 experience.

Package: wildos-fonts
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, fontconfig
Description: Albert Sans, the Wild OS typeface
 The variable Albert Sans fonts, upright and italic, under the SIL Open
 Font Licence. Debian does not package them; every Wild OS app, the
 installer and the desktop are set in them.
